{'metadata': {'total_results': None, 'truncated_results': 0, 'truncated_companies': 0, 'total_companies': None}, 'data': [{'id': 610803699, 'job_title': 'Venture Growth', 'url': 'https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/paraform/daa0f2d9-500d-4bb7-b1bb-c75a36369162?src=LinkedIn', 'date_posted': '2026-01-25', 'has_blurred_data': False, 'company': 'Paraform', 'final_url': 'https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/paraform/daa0f2d9-500d-4bb7-b1bb-c75a36369162?src=LinkedIn', 'source_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/venture-growth-at-paraform-4365746429', 'location': 'San Francisco, CA', 'short_location': 'San Francisco, CA', 'long_location': 'San Francisco, CA', 'state_code': 'CA', 'latitude': 37.77493, 'longitude': -122.41942, 'postal_code': None, 'remote': False, 'hybrid': False, 'salary_string': None, 'min_annual_salary': None, 'min_annual_salary_usd': None, 'max_annual_salary': None, 'max_annual_salary_usd': None, 'avg_annual_salary_usd': None, 'salary_currency': None, 'countries': [], 'country': 'United States', 'country_codes': ['US'], 'country_code': 'US', 'cities': [], 'continents': [], 'seniority': 'mid_level', 'discovered_at': '2026-01-25T13:10:05.547000Z', 'company_domain': 'paraform.com', 'hiring_team': [], 'reposted': False, 'date_reposted': None, 'employment_statuses': ['full_time'], 'easy_apply': None, 'technology_slugs': ['ashby'], 'description': "**We're seeking a highly motivated investor to lead Venture Growth as a founding member of our GTM team.**\nCursor, Decagon, Windsurf and 300+ other leading startups hire their hardest roles with Paraform. During the past 3 months, we piloted a program to grow this startup customer base through partnerships with leading VC firms including Menlo, 8VC, Felicis, Sutter Hill Ventures, and A\\* Capital. Already, dozens of startups referred through these relationships have made critical hires for their early teams using Paraform.\n  \n  \nOur Venture Growth lead will convert this momentum into a scalable program.\n  \n  \n**What We Look For**\n\n- 4 - 6 years of experience in investing or high-growth startups\n- Experience building relationships with VC firms, accelerators, or startup communities.\n- Strong understanding of the startup ecosystem, especially early-stage fundraising and founder needs.\n- Excellent communicator—can confidently represent the company to top-tier VCs\n\n**What You'll Do**\n\n- Form and manage partnerships with top venture investors, accelerators, and other partners in the startup ecosystem\n- Work across the Paraform organization to help startups accelerate their progress and be successful using our platform.\n- Identify and execute on partnership opportunities with investors outside of tech to scale Paraform into new market\n\n**About Paraform**\nParaform is a marketplace modernizing one of the largest and most fragmented markets in the world: hiring.\n**We partner with industry leaders like Cursor, Palantir, Windsurf, Decagon, Shopify, Coinbase, and Hightouch**\nto hire world-class talent, and are growing quickly -\n**8×-ing revenue last year.**\nParaform is the first end-to-end AI recruiting marketplace that connects companies with thousands of specialized recruiters and AI agents that work together to fill roles faster and more accurately.\n  \n  \nOur mission is to make hiring fast, reliable, and scalable for every company in the world.\n  \n  \nAt Paraform, we believe recruiting works best when the right people are working on the right problems, combining human judgment with AI that truly understands hiring. That’s why we’re building a new foundation for how companies hire, bringing together specialized recruiters and modern AI tools.\n  \n  \nWe treat recruiters like entrepreneurs, not vendors – and we’re building the financial, operational, and technical infrastructure that powers their success.\n  \n  \nWe are backed by the best investors and technology leaders: Felicis, A\\*, BOND, Liquid 2, DST Global, the founders of YouTube, Instacart, Canva, and more.", 'company_object': {'id': 'YqJe4MRudmQcMjoMV8aNlg==', 'name': 'Paraform', 'domain': 'paraform.com', 'industry': 'Internet Marketplace Platforms', 'country': 'United States', 'country_code': 'US', 'employee_count': 260, 'logo': 'https://media.theirstack.com/company/logo/domain/paraform.com.jpeg', 'num_jobs': 84, 'num_technologies': 40, 'possible_domains': ['paraform.com'], 'url': 'https://paraform.com', 'industry_id': 1285, 'linkedin_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/paraformxyz/', 'num_jobs_last_30_days': 1, 'num_jobs_found': None, 'yc_batch': None, 'apollo_id': '62d56990e5f4be00b32104b6', 'linkedin_id': '86609201', 'url_source': None, 'is_recruiting_agency': False, 'founded_year': 2022, 'annual_revenue_usd': None, 'annual_revenue_usd_readable': None, 'total_funding_usd': 1400000, 'last_funding_round_date': '2024-04-15', 'last_funding_round_amount_readable': '$1.4M', 'employee_count_range': '201-500', 'long_description': "Paraform is a marketplace connecting companies with open roles and recruiters who can fill them.\n\nCompanies can work with specialized recruiters more cheaply, monitor their performance, and flex based on demand. Recruiters don't have to worry about acquiring clients while earning and working on their own terms.\n\nIncredible teams at the most exciting startups and enterprises are being built as a result.", 'seo_description': 'Get paid to recruit for the most exciting startups on your own terms. Recruiting has never been so accessible.', 'city': 'San Francisco', 'postal_code': '94102', 'company_keywords': [], 'alexa_ranking': 250453, 'publicly_traded_symbol': None, 'publicly_traded_exchange': None, 'investors': ['Primer Sazze Partners'], 'funding_stage': 'seed', 'has_blurred_data': False, 'technology_slugs': [], 'technology_names': []}, 'locations': [{'id': 5391959, 'name': 'San Francisco', 'type': 'city', 'feature_code': 'PPLA2', 'country_code': 'US', 'admin1_name': 'California', 'admin1_code': 'CA', 'admin2_name': '075', 'admin2_code': '075', 'continent': 'NA', 'latitude': 37.77493, 'longitude': -122.41942, 'city': 'San Francisco', 'address': None, 'postal_code': None, 'state': 'California', 'state_code': 'CA', 'display_name': 'San Francisco, California, United States', 'country_name': 'United States'}], 'normalized_title': '', 'manager_roles': [], 'matching_phrases': [], 'matching_words': []}, {'id': 610734246, 'job_title': 'Insurance & Billing Strategy Consultant', 'url': 'https://www.sanfranciscogigs.com/job.asp?aff=5F88FB33-7ECC-414D-823B-00B1224EBD09&id=3138983249', 'date_posted': '2026-01-25', 'has_blurred_data': False, 'company': 'Mochi Health', 'final_url': None, 'source_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/insurance-billing-strategy-consultant-at-mochi-health-4365758002', 'location': 'San Francisco Bay Area', 'short_location': 'San Francisco Bay Area', 'long_location': 'San Francisco Bay Area', 'state_code': None, 'latitude': 37.39271, 'longitude': -122.042, 'postal_code': None, 'remote': False, 'hybrid': False, 'salary_string': None, 'min_annual_salary': None, 'min_annual_salary_usd': None, 'max_annual_salary': None, 'max_annual_salary_usd': None, 'avg_annual_salary_usd': None, 'salary_currency': None, 'countries': [], 'country': 'United States', 'country_codes': ['US'], 'country_code': 'US', 'cities': [], 'continents': [], 'seniority': 'mid_level', 'discovered_at': '2026-01-25T09:11:34.716000Z', 'company_domain': 'joinmochi.com', 'hiring_team': [], 'reposted': False, 'date_reposted': None, 'employment_statuses': ['full_time'], 'easy_apply': None, 'technology_slugs': [], 'description': "Mochi Health's mission is to be the discovery layer of healthcare. We are building a platform that makes it easier for patients to find the right providers, access the right medications, and take control of their health with transparency and trust.\n  \n  \nOver the past few years, we have experienced rapid growth by combining operational excellence, clinical expertise, and innovative technology to deliver care that is more human, intuitive, and effective. From pharmacy pricing transparency and personalized medication management, to long-term medical record access and community-based chronic illness support, Mochi is creating a new model of care that empowers patients, providers, and pharmacies alike.\n  \n  \nWe believe the future of healthcare is personal, and we are building the technology to power it. At Mochi Health, you will join a team that values inclusivity, collaboration, and bold thinking, and you will have the opportunity to do the most meaningful work of your career.\n  \n  \n**Engagement Type:**\nContract\n  \n  \n**Duration:**\n3-6 months (with potential for extension)\n  \n  \n**Commitment:**\n10-20 hours/week\n  \n  \n**About Mochi Health**\nMochi Health's mission is to be the discovery layer of healthcare. We are building a platform that makes it easier for patients to find the right providers, access the right medications, and take control of their health with transparency and trust.\n  \n  \nOver the past few years, we have experienced rapid growth by combining operational excellence, clinical expertise, and innovative technology to deliver care that is more human, intuitive, and effective. From pharmacy pricing transparency and personalized medication management, to long-term medical record access and community-based chronic illness support, Mochi is creating a new model of care that empowers patients, providers, and pharmacies alike.\n  \n  \nWe believe the future of healthcare is personal, and we are building the technology to power it. At Mochi Health, you will join a team that values inclusivity, collaboration, and bold thinking, and you will have the opportunity to do the most meaningful work of your career.\n  \n  \n**About The Role**\nWe're seeking an experienced insurance and billing consultant to advise on our expansion of insurance offerings and optimization of revenue cycle operations. This role will provide strategic guidance on payer relations, contract negotiations, billing compliance, and reimbursement optimization as we scale our insurance product.\n  \n  \n**What You'll Do**\n\n- Advise on payer contracting strategy and negotiations with commercial insurers â€¢ Review and optimize current payer relations and revenue cycle workflows including eligibility verification and payment posting\n- Provide guidance on billing compliance and coding optimization for telehealth services â€¢ Support development of claims management processes and denial reduction strategies â€¢ Advise on reimbursement strategies across multiple payer types and state regulations â€¢ Guide insurance product development and go-to-market strategy for new coverage offerings\n- Provide strategic recommendations on payer mix optimization and network expansion Required Qualifications\n- 5+ years experience in healthcare payer relations, insurance operations, and revenue cycle management, ideally specific to telehealth\n- Deep expertise in medical billing, coding, and reimbursement for commercial payers â€¢ Proven track record negotiating payer contracts and managing payer relationships â€¢ Strong understanding of telehealth billing regulations and compliance requirements â€¢ Experience with claims processing, denial management, and appeals â€¢ Experience with CMS regulations, Medicare billing requirements, and federal reimbursement programs\n\n**Nice To Have**\n\n- Experience with revenue cycle management platforms such as Candid Health or similar billing automation tools\n- Familiarity with clearinghouse operations and payer connectivity platforms like Availity Who You Are\n- Deep experience across payer contracting, credentialing, claims processing, and revenue cycle management. You understand how commercial payers, Medicare, and state programs operate.\n- Current on healthcare billing regulations, compliance requirements, and payer policies across multiple states.\n- Proven track record negotiating with payers and collaborating across clinical, finance, and operations teams.\n- You use analytics to optimize reimbursement, reduce denials, and improve performance. â€¢ You deliver results in fast-moving environments with shifting priorities.\n\n**Workplace Policy**\nMochi Health is an in-person company based in San Francisco, CA. Our team works together in person five days a week to foster collaboration, innovation, and strong connections. We believe that face-to-face interaction builds a culture of excellence and allows us to deliver the best outcomes for the patients and providers we serve.\n  \n  \nFor office-based roles, the standard schedule is Monday through Friday, 9:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. Actual hours may vary depending on business needs and role responsibilities. All employees receive meal and rest breaks in accordance with applicable state and local laws.\n  \n  \nFor designated remote roles, this in-person policy does not apply.\n  \n  \n**Equal Opportunity**\nMochi Health is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We make all employment decisions based solely on merit. We provide equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees without discrimination on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, disability status, or any other applicable legally protected characteristic. We prohibit any form of discrimination or harassment. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including hiring.\n  \n  \n**Candidate Privacy Notice**\nPlease review Mochi Health's Candidate Privacy Notice here\n  \n  \n**Accommodations**\nMochi Health complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), as amended by the ADA Amendments Act, and all applicable state or local laws. We will reasonably accommodate qualified individuals with a disability during the application process and throughout employment as required by law.\n  \n  \nIf you need any assistance or accommodations due to a disability, please contact us at\n**hr@joinmochi.com**", 'company_object': {'id': '4YxjdmK9TD9+TG94afvo5A==', 'name': 'Mochi Health', 'domain': 'joinmochi.com', 'industry': 'Hospitals and Health Care', 'country': 'United States', 'country_code': 'US', 'employee_count': 290, 'logo': 'https://media.theirstack.com/company/logo/domain/joinmochi.com.jpeg', 'num_jobs': 693, 'num_technologies': 108, 'possible_domains': ['joinmochi.com'], 'url': 'https://joinmochi.com', 'industry_id': 14, 'linkedin_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/mochihealth/', 'num_jobs_last_30_days': 19, 'num_jobs_found': None, 'yc_batch': None, 'apollo_id': None, 'linkedin_id': '78397379', 'url_source': None, 'is_recruiting_agency': False, 'founded_year': None, 'annual_revenue_usd': None, 'annual_revenue_usd_readable': None, 'total_funding_usd': None, 'last_funding_round_date': '2022-03-14', 'last_funding_round_amount_readable': None, 'employee_count_range': '201-500', 'long_description': "We're Mochi Health, a pioneering force in obesity medicine dedicated to building personalized, clinically-backed weight care solutions. We're on a mission to empower patients with one-on-one virtual care and proven pharmaceutical treatments.\n\nWe recognize that every body is unique, and believe weight loss plans should be, too.\n\nWith over 100 million individuals struggling with obesity and 15 million already using GLP-1 prescriptions, the need for specialized guidance is at an all-time high. We help patients navigate their treatments and achieve lasting success by connecting them with board-certified providers, dietitians, and access to our support team around the clock. Our best-in-class telehealth platform is designed to make care accessible to patients whenever and wherever they need it.\n\nAt Mochi Health, we believe that our success is driven by the people we hire. Join us in shaping the future of obesity medicine and transforming the lives of millions of patients.", 'seo_description': 'Customize your weight loss journey: board-certified obesity medicine doctors, nutritionists, and fitness coaches.', 'city': 'San Francisco', 'postal_code': '94105', 'company_keywords': [], 'alexa_ranking': None, 'publicly_traded_symbol': None, 'publicly_traded_exchange': None, 'investors': [], 'funding_stage': 'pre_seed', 'has_blurred_data': False, 'technology_slugs': [], 'technology_names': []}, 'locations': [], 'normalized_title': '', 'manager_roles': [], 'matching_phrases': [], 'matching_words': []}, {'id': 610799778, 'job_title': 'Venture Banking Credit Analyst (Summer 2026 Start)', 'url': 'https://careers-stifel.icims.com/jobs/8081/venture-banking-credit-analyst-(summer-2026-start)/job?iis=LinkedIn&in_iframe=1&mode=apply', 'date_posted': '2026-01-25', 'has_blurred_data': False, 'company': 'Stifel Financial Corp.', 'final_url': 'https://careers-stifel.icims.com/jobs/8081/venture-banking-credit-analyst-(summer-2026-start)/job?iis=LinkedIn&in_iframe=1&mode=apply', 'source_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/venture-banking-credit-analyst-summer-2026-start-at-stifel-financial-corp-4320311107', 'location': 'San Francisco, CA', 'short_location': 'San Francisco, CA', 'long_location': 'San Francisco, CA', 'state_code': 'CA', 'latitude': 37.77493, 'longitude': -122.41942, 'postal_code': None, 'remote': False, 'hybrid': False, 'salary_string': '$80k - $100k per year', 'min_annual_salary': 80000, 'min_annual_salary_usd': 80000.0, 'max_annual_salary': 100000, 'max_annual_salary_usd': 100000.0, 'avg_annual_salary_usd': 90000.0, 'salary_currency': 'USD', 'countries': [], 'country': 'United States', 'country_codes': ['US'], 'country_code': 'US', 'cities': [], 'continents': [], 'seniority': 'mid_level', 'discovered_at': '2026-01-25T12:54:46.013000Z', 'company_domain': 'stifel.com', 'hiring_team': [], 'reposted': False, 'date_reposted': None, 'employment_statuses': ['full_time'], 'easy_apply': None, 'technology_slugs': ['microsoft-excel', 'microsoft-powerpoint', 'microsoft-outlook', 'component', 'icims'], 'description': "**Why Stifel**\nStifel strives for a culture that puts its clients and associates first: a culture where everyone belongs, everyone is welcome, and everyone contributes to the success of our clients, their careers, and the firm as a whole.\n  \n  \nLet’s talk about how you can find your place here at Stifel,\n**where success meets success**\n.\n  \n  \n**What You'll Be Doing**\nThe Venture Banking Credit Analyst will be an integral part of origination, underwriting, and portfolio management. This position will be responsible for banking and lending directly to private investment funds across several asset classes. The Credit Analyst will have exposure to many different business units while creating a differentiated market strategy.\n  \n  \n**What We're Looking For**\n\n- Assist in managing the deal process from origination and underwriting to execution.\n- Collect and review diligence materials to prepare credit memorandums for presentation to the leadership team.\n- Monitor an existing portfolio of borrowers to ensure compliance with loan covenants and report status up to the leadership team.\n- Maintain in-depth knowledge to creatively evolve processes and procedures to enhance efficiency and scalability.\n- Remain an active participant in the fund finance ecosystem to become an expert in banking and lending to private funds.\n- Identify opportunities for process improvements.\n\n**What You'll Bring**\n\n- Knowledge of how private closed-end funds operate and the multiple entities involved (limited partners, general partner, etc.).\n- Strong skills and experience in analyzing investments funds and their underlying objectives.\n- Knowledge of key financial principles.\n- Strong ability to produce high quality work products independently and as part of a collegial team.\n- Comfort in working directly with senior executives and investment Firms.\n- Ability to work in an entrepreneurial culture with the desire to figure out how to solve problems and execute.\n\n**Education & Experience**\n\n- Minimum Required: Bachelor's Degree in finance, accounting or another business related field.\n- Minimum Required: 1-3 years' of commercial banking, investment banking, or private capital investing experience.\n\n**Licenses & Credentials**\n\n- Minimum Required: None\n\n**Systems & Technology**\n\n- Proficient in Microsoft Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook\n\n**Compensation Range**\nSalary: USD $80,000.00/Yr. - USD $100,000.00/Yr.\n  \n  \nActual salaries may vary, and may be based on several factors, including but not limited to each candidate’s qualifications, skills, and overall competencies for the position. The base salary is one component of Stifel’s overall compensation package for each individual employee. Other benefits and offerings include, but not limited to, discretionary bonuses, health / dental / vision / prescription insurance offerings, Stifel Total Health Connect, flexible spending accounts, tuition & certification assistance programs, paid time off, and much, much more! To view a more comprehensive list of Stifel’s current offerings, please visit https://www.stifel.com/careers/benefits. Applications are accepted until the position is filled.\n  \n  \n**About Stifel**\nStifel is more than 130 years old and still thinking like a start-up. We are a global wealth management and investment banking firm serious about innovation and fresh ideas. Built on a simple premise of safeguarding our clients’ money as if it were our own, coined by our namesake, Herman Stifel, our success is intimately tied to our commitment to helping families, companies, and municipalities find their own success.\n  \n  \nWhile our headquarters is in St. Louis, we have offices in New York, San Francisco, Baltimore, London, Frankfurt, Toronto, and more than 400 other locations. Stifel is home to approximately 9,000 individuals who are currently building their careers as financial advisors, research analysts, project managers, marketing specialists, developers, bankers, operations associates, among hundreds more. Let’s talk about how you can find your place here at Stifel, where success meets success.\n  \n  \nAt Stifel we offer an entrepreneurial environment, comprehensive benefits package to include health, dental and vision care, 401k, wellness initiatives, life insurance, and paid time off.\n  \n  \nStifel’s bank and trust companies are equal opportunity employers. All candidates will be considered without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, marital status, veteran status, genetic information or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. If you would like more information regarding Equal Employment Opportunity rights and protections, please review the following information: Know Your Rights.\n  \n  \nStifel is an Equal Opportunity Employer.", 'company_object': {'id': 'njBs+UPzECYTQdEbPQ7yKlMaBv+ChBshOHyQJDOsX6g=', 'name': 'Stifel Financial Corp.', 'domain': 'stifel.com', 'industry': 'Financial Services', 'country': 'United States', 'country_code': 'US', 'employee_count': 8600, 'logo': 'https://media.theirstack.com/company/logo/domain/stifel.com.jpeg', 'num_jobs': 1084, 'num_technologies': 203, 'possible_domains': ['stifel.com'], 'url': 'https://stifel.com', 'industry_id': 43, 'linkedin_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/stifel-financial-corp-/', 'num_jobs_last_30_days': 47, 'num_jobs_found': None, 'yc_batch': None, 'apollo_id': '5569d03e736964259ca89900', 'linkedin_id': '10194', 'url_source': None, 'is_recruiting_agency': False, 'founded_year': 1890, 'annual_revenue_usd': 4381705000.0, 'annual_revenue_usd_readable': '4.4B', 'total_funding_usd': None, 'last_funding_round_date': None, 'last_funding_round_amount_readable': None, 'employee_count_range': '5001-10,000', 'long_description': "Established in 1890, Stifel, Nicolaus & Company, Incorporated is one of the nation’s premier full-service financial services firms, providing brokerage, trading, investment banking, investment advisory, and related services to individual investors, professional money managers, businesses, and municipalities through more than 400 locations across the U.S.\n \nStifel ranks as the 7th largest brokerage firm in the country as measured by number of financial advisors, with approximately 2,300, and features a highly regarded equity research department that has earned numerous accolades from such publications as The Wall Street Journal, Forbes, and the Financial Times. In 2023 and 2024, Stifel was recognized as the No. 1 wealth management firm for employee advisor satisfaction, based on the J.D. Power U.S. Financial Advisor Satisfaction Study*.\n \nStifel is the principal subsidiary of Stifel Financial Corp. (NYSE: SF), a financial services holding company headquartered in St. Louis, Missouri. Stifel Financial Corp.'s other subsidiaries include Stifel Independent Advisors, LLC, an independent contractor broker-dealer firm; Stifel Nicolaus Europe Limited, the Company’s European subsidiary; Stifel Nicolaus Canada, Inc., our Canadian subsidiary; Stifel Bank and Trust and Stifel Bank, retail and commercial banks; and Stifel Trust Company, N.A. and Stifel Trust Company Delaware, N.A, our trust companies.\n\n*Stifel received the highest score among employee advisors in the J.D. Power 2023-2024 U.S. Financial Advisor Satisfaction Studies, which measures employee advisors’ satisfaction among those who are employed by an investment services firm. Visit jdpower.com/awards for more details.", 'seo_description': 'Stifel is a full service brokerage and investment banking firm. The Company provides securities brokerage, investment banking, trading, investment advisory, and related financial services to individual investors, professional money managers, businesses, and municipalities.', 'city': 'St. Louis', 'postal_c